# ECS DOTS Rule

Read `.cursor/packs/unity-game/guides/ecs-dots.md` before writing or reviewing any ECS system, component, or authoring.

Key rules (NON-NEGOTIABLE):

- No `EntityManager.CreateEntity()` without a prefab source — use Authoring + Baker pattern.
- Every entity has an Authoring MonoBehaviour and a matching Baker inner class.
- Runtime config data is written by Systems, not Bakers.
- Component naming: data → no suffix, tag → `Tag`, cleanup → `CleanupData`, managed ref → `Reference`.
- Structural changes (`AddComponent`, `RemoveComponent`, `DestroyEntity`) inside systems MUST use `EntityCommandBuffer`.
- `ISystem` (Burst) uses `IJobEntity` + `ScheduleParallel` — NOT `foreach`.
- `SystemBase` acts as the managed bridge — Mono ↔ ECS goes through `SystemBase`, not directly to `ISystem`.
- Every system declares `[UpdateInGroup]` explicitly — no implicit default group.
- ECS code lives in `Ecs/Authorings/`, `Ecs/Components/`, `Ecs/Systems/` — never in `Abstracts/` or `Concretes/`.
